{
  "_comment": "scx#3618 repro: a directly cpu.max-limited cgroup (125us quota per 100ms period = 0.125% of one CPU) holding one compute hog and eight repeatedly-waking short victims, plus an unlimited competitor in the root cgroup whose continued progress shows the machine is not merely saturated. Run with -s lavd and --sched-config enabling enable_cpu_bw. Demonstrates the unbounded bandwidth wait of https://github.com/sched-ext/scx/pull/3618.",
  "_run_units": "rt-app run/sleep are microseconds; cpu.max is '<quota_us> <period_us>'. NOTE: 'duration' is parsed with as_i64 \u2014 a FLOAT here is silently ignored and replaced by the 10s default.",
